# The eval scene set: goal, spawn bound, and why. ONE place, so no hand-written
# command can drop a parameter again.
#
# SPAWN_MAX matters: with a FIXED goal frame, a spawn drawn AFTER that frame puts
# the goal behind a forward-only robot, which then needs a ~164 deg spin before it
# can move at all. Every arm failed quad2_00 episode 1 for exactly this reason
# (2026-09-23, Joana spotted it in the trajectories).
#
# SPAWN_MAX alone is not enough for a CORNER test: spawning 8 frames before the
# goal puts the robot past the bend, so there is nothing to turn around. The old
# correct runs were named spawn12-22_goal48 -- 26-36 frames of approach, so the
# robot must reach the bend, turn, and continue (2026-09-23, Joana).
#
# MEASURED with scripts/scene_bend.py, not copied off an old folder name:
#   quad2_00     bend at frames 25-45;  spawn 12-22 -> 254 deg of turning to the goal, 13 deg inside
#   sequoia1_17  bend starts at frame 50; 40-56 put 58 deg INSIDE the spawn range, so 34-48 instead
#
# TESTDIST (2026-09-24) is the distance the test ACTUALLY spans, in metres, taken
# from the mean d_start of runs that have already gone through. Without it the
# episode budget is sized from each ARM's curriculum reach, so on the identical
# 8.1 m far corner chunk5 (reach 4 m) got 104 actions and memDINO_warm (reach
# 7.5 m) got 160 -- and 104 actions cannot cover 8.1 m at any throttle chunk5 has
# shown. Its TIMEOUT was the budget, not the policy (Joana: "this one seems to
# time out too early"). A short test never shrinks a longer curriculum's budget.
#
# format:  <scene> <goal spec> <spawn bounds, comma separated, or ->   # note
EVAL_SCENES="
quad1_01     GOALFRAMERANGE=15,70   -        TESTDIST=8.4   # open plaza; graded, 3.9-8.4 m measured
quad1_07     GOALFRAMERANGE=15,70   -        TESTDIST=8.4   # second plaza (duplicate of quad1_01, usually skip)
quad2_00     GOAL_FRAME=48          SPAWN_MIN=12,SPAWN_MAX=22   TESTDIST=5.4   # corner: spawn WELL BEFORE the bend
sequoia1_10  GOAL_FRAME=30          SPAWN_MIN=5,SPAWN_MAX=18    TESTDIST=3.9   # pedestrians, NOT in training
sequoia1_17  GOAL_FRAME=72          SPAWN_MIN=34,SPAWN_MAX=48   # lawn corner; bend starts at frame 50
quad2_00_far GOAL_FRAME=55          SPAWN_MIN=5,SPAWN_MAX=12    SCENE=quad2_00 TESTDIST=8.1  # LONG corner: spawn 2.2-3.0 m
                                                                                # along, bend at 6.8-10.8 m,
                                                                                # goal at 13.6 m -- the turn is
                                                                                # unmistakable on a path plot
"

# gnd -- the only HONESTLY held-out environment. Every campus clip sits within 30 m
# of a training clip, so no campus scene is truly out of distribution; gnd is a
# different site entirely. Frames there are 0.38 m apart against campus's 0.23-0.37,
# so a goal frame chosen by campus habit lands far outside the trained band -- these
# were measured with scripts/scene_bend.py to sit at 5.3-7.9 m (2026-09-24).
# Clips live in data/gnd_clips, not campus_clips, hence the CLIPS= column.
EVAL_SCENES_GND="
gnd_AU_180   GOAL_FRAME=32   SPAWN_MIN=10,SPAWN_MAX=16  CLIPS=gnd_clips TESTDIST=6.9  # 21 deg and the straight line is walkable: OPEN navigation, not a corner
gnd_AUw360   GOAL_FRAME=40   SPAWN_MIN=13,SPAWN_MAX=18  CLIPS=gnd_clips TESTDIST=6.1  # the WALK turns 151 deg but nothing blocks the straight line: an open turn, so it does not test obstacle avoidance (Joana, 2026-09-24)
# BROKEN, do not run until re-measured: spawn frames 20-25 sit on GRASS, so all 16
# episodes of both arms crashed at step 1-2 while the goal was on traversable ground
# (2026-09-24, Joana: it starts on grass). scene_bend.py could not catch this -- it
# reads poses only. Re-measure with:  python scripts/scene_corner_scan.py gnd_AUw170
# gnd_AUw170   GOAL_FRAME=45   SPAWN_MIN=20,SPAWN_MAX=25  CLIPS=gnd_clips TESTDIST=7.0
"
EVAL_SCENES="${EVAL_SCENES}${EVAL_SCENES_GND}"

# The three-scene core set: open navigation, turning, and a scene held out of training.
EVAL_CORE="quad1_01 quad2_00 sequoia1_10"
# The held-out set: one open, two corners, a different site.
# AUw170 is out until its spawn window is re-measured; AUw360 is an OPEN turn, so
# neither held-out scene currently tests turning around an obstacle. Finding one is
# what scene_corner_scan.py is for.
EVAL_GND="gnd_AU_180 gnd_AUw360"
